<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>World news and headlines - RFI</title><description>Follow any political information, cultural, sporting and live streaming on RFI. The latest information, news and events in France, Europe and around the world.</description><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/</link><lastBuildDate>Mon, 17 Aug 2026 09:50:56 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>International</category><title>Migrants stranded in Ceuta say ‘I’d rather die here than go back to Morocco’</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260817-migrants-stranded-in-ceuta-say-i-d-rather-die-here-than-go-back-to-morocco</link><description>
Nearly three weeks after a mass border crossing brought tens of thousands of migrants into Spain's North African enclave of Ceuta, thousands remain stranded in precarious conditions, Maria Jimenez, spokesperson for the NGO Elin, told RFI. She said many still lack adequate shelter, food and medical care.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/49488ca8-9a1a-11f1-ab02-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26227626392783.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/49488ca8-9a1a-11f1-ab02-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26227626392783.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3eca97cc-9a19-11f1-8e9f-33840bc1377b</guid><pubDate>Mon, 17 Aug 2026 09:48:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/49488ca8-9a1a-11f1-ab02-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26227626392783.jpg">AP Photo/STR - STR</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Belgium turns to European air support as wildfire rages near German border</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260816-belgium-turns-to-european-air-support-as-wildfire-rages-near-german-border</link><description>
Belgium called in aerial reinforcements from across Europe on Sunday as firefighters battled the country’s largest wildfire in more than a century, with flames spreading rapidly through a difficult-to-reach nature reserve near the German border.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/baaa53f4-996b-11f1-ba0b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Belgium-Wildfire.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/baaa53f4-996b-11f1-ba0b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Belgium-Wildfire.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cdccd256-9955-11f1-9ad6-2b9ea6a90619</guid><pubDate>Sun, 16 Aug 2026 12:24:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/baaa53f4-996b-11f1-ba0b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Belgium-Wildfire.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Morocco arrests nearly 300 migrants near Ceuta amid renewed crossing fears</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260816-morocco-arrests-nearly-300-migrants-near-ceuta-amid-renewed-crossing-fears</link><description>
Scores of would-be migrants, most of them from sub-Saharan Africa, were intercepted in northern Morocco near the border with the Spanish exclave of Ceuta on Saturday, two weeks after tens of thousands of people attempted to enter the territory.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/565461a6-9731-11f1-9694-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26215527124781.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/565461a6-9731-11f1-9694-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26215527124781.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">796023ce-9957-11f1-bc95-7f396f569dcf</guid><pubDate>Sun, 16 Aug 2026 10:13:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/565461a6-9731-11f1-9694-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26215527124781.jpg">AP Photo/Bernat Armangue - Bernat Armangue</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Armenian Genocide survivors' grandson says 'political motives' block recognition</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260815-armenian-survivor-s-grandson-says-politics-still-blocks-genocide-recognition</link><description>
In 1915, the Ottoman Empire began the systematic deportation and massacre of its Armenian population. As many as 1.5 million Armenians were killed – widely regarded by historians as the twentieth century's first genocide, and the event for which the term was later coined. Stephan Pechdimaldji, the grandson of two of the survivors, spoke to RFI about why recognition still matters.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/656fb228-a554-11eb-a73b-005056bf87d6/w:1024/p:16x9/063_1314238954.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/656fb228-a554-11eb-a73b-005056bf87d6/w:1024/p:16x9/063_1314238954.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">221a786c-969b-11f1-83af-a5d44a90634e</guid><pubDate>Sat, 15 Aug 2026 19:03:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/656fb228-a554-11eb-a73b-005056bf87d6/w:1024/p:16x9/063_1314238954.jpg">Getty Images via AFP - MARIO TAMA</source><dc:creator>Jan van der Made</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Nine killed in Israeli strikes on Lebanon as tensions test peace framework</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260815-nine-killed-in-israeli-strikes-on-lebanon-as-tensions-test-peace-framework</link><description>
At least nine people were killed in Israeli strikes on southern Lebanon on Saturday, according to Lebanon’s state news agency, in some of the deadliest attacks since Beirut agreed to a US-mediated framework aimed at ending the latest round of fighting.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/498bb8d2-989b-11f1-a70f-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Lebanon-Strike-bu-Israel.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/498bb8d2-989b-11f1-a70f-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Lebanon-Strike-bu-Israel.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">70f27d30-989a-11f1-b0c2-51a8ef8c8f74</guid><pubDate>Sat, 15 Aug 2026 13:14:08 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/498bb8d2-989b-11f1-a70f-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Lebanon-Strike-bu-Israel.jpg">© Mahmoud ZAYYAT / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International report</category><title>In Turkey, one of the world's longest conflicts reaches a turning point</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/podcasts/international-report/20260815-in-turkey-one-of-the-world-s-longest-conflicts-reaches-a-turning-point</link><description>
Turkey stands on the threshold of closing a conflict spanning almost 50 years, after the Turkish parliament this week passed a law allowing exiled Kurdish militants to return home and rejoin society. The legislation aims to end the war with the Kurdistan Workers' Party (PKK), which has battled the Turkish state for independence since 1984.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e4d800d6-f5ed-11ef-8568-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24155534800968.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e4d800d6-f5ed-11ef-8568-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24155534800968.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">050704c0-97e5-11f1-9f60-61ddff2f7428</guid><pubDate>Sat, 15 Aug 2026 10:52:06 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Dorian Jones</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Five years into Taliban rule, Afghanistan seeks to ease international isolation</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260815-five-years-into-taliban-rule-afghanistan-seeks-to-ease-international-isolation</link><description>
In the five years since the Taliban seized back power in Afghanistan, the country's worsening human rights record has drawn sanctions and aid cuts. But despite refusing to officially recognise the fundamentalist movement's government, some countries are concluding that engaging with the Taliban has become unavoidable.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c3a283ec-6be8-11f1-bfd3-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26072483578608-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c3a283ec-6be8-11f1-bfd3-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26072483578608-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d87aa374-96f1-11f1-938b-1bb6596caa4b</guid><pubDate>Sat, 15 Aug 2026 07:21:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c3a283ec-6be8-11f1-bfd3-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26072483578608-1.jpg">© AP - Hedayat Shah </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Fake accounts and false rumours drive new Ceuta crossing campaign</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260814-fake-accounts-and-false-rumours-drive-new-ceuta-crossing-campaign</link><description>
Calls for a new mass crossing into Ceuta, a Spanish enclave on Morocco's Mediterranean coast, have flooded Moroccan social media, with posts urging migrants to rush the border on Saturday. An RFI investigation found the campaign was fuelled by false rumours, suspicious accounts and signs of artificial amplification.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/74e6b070-972b-11f1-af60-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Ceuta-15-aout-Espagne-Maroc-1.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/74e6b070-972b-11f1-af60-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Ceuta-15-aout-Espagne-Maroc-1.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a3e28e4a-97f2-11f1-990a-af55d9f4e9ef</guid><pubDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 16:04:02 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/74e6b070-972b-11f1-af60-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Ceuta-15-aout-Espagne-Maroc-1.png">© Screengrabs compiled by RFI</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Europe faces rocket shortage by 2030 as satellite demand surges</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260814-europe-faces-rocket-shortage-by-2030-as-satellite-demand-surges</link><description>
Europe could face a shortage of rockets to launch its satellites by the end of the decade as demand for access to space rises sharply, the head of the European Space Agency has warned.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/45b4d134-7822-11f0-a644-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%BA%D0%B5%D1%82%D0%B0-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/45b4d134-7822-11f0-a644-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%BA%D0%B5%D1%82%D0%B0-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">372c3fca-966d-11f1-89f6-1d0544cfefef</guid><pubDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 13:58:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/45b4d134-7822-11f0-a644-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%BA%D0%B5%D1%82%D0%B0-1.jpg">© ESA - European Space Agency</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Controversial Covid-19 study retracted over links to vaccine misinformation</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260814-controversial-covid-19-study-retracted-over-links-to-vaccine-misinformation</link><description>
A controversial study analysing excess deaths during the Covid-19 pandemic has been retracted, after being widely criticised for lending credence to vaccine scepticism.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/84541958-dbde-11ef-a875-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/MYSTER~1.PNG"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/84541958-dbde-11ef-a875-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/MYSTER~1.PNG" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c4fae552-9647-11f1-953c-75761acc26ea</guid><pubDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 12:23:56 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/84541958-dbde-11ef-a875-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/MYSTER~1.PNG">© REUTERS/File photo</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>A war on words: why Russian strikes are targeting Ukrainian publishers</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260813-a-war-on-words-why-russian-strikes-are-targeting-ukrainian-publishers</link><description>
On 1 August Russian drone strikes on a logistics and distribution centre in northern Kharkiv destroyed more than 8 million books, in a war being waged not just at the frontline, but on Ukraine's culture and identity.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c79bb66c-9708-11f1-ae73-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Kharkiv-Book-Destruction-11.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c79bb66c-9708-11f1-ae73-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Kharkiv-Book-Destruction-11.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fdca3af2-9707-11f1-ade3-2b17bfcbc78a</guid><pubDate>Thu, 13 Aug 2026 19:51:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c79bb66c-9708-11f1-ae73-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Kharkiv-Book-Destruction-11.jpg">© Emmanuelle Chaze</source><dc:creator>Emmanuelle Chaze</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>France and 30 other countries condemn Iran's executions of protestors</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260813-france-and-30-other-countries-condemn-iran-s-executions-of-protestors</link><description>
More than 30 countries, including France, the United Kingdom and Canada, have condemned Iran's use of capital punishment, saying in a joint statement on Wednesday the Islamic Republic was executing protesters to "silence dissent". Tehran accused its critics of hypocrisy.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/895cb972-373c-11f1-ac98-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26079799726369.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/895cb972-373c-11f1-ac98-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26079799726369.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bc38027c-96f8-11f1-a728-1bb6596caa4b</guid><pubDate>Thu, 13 Aug 2026 15:02:28 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/895cb972-373c-11f1-ac98-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26079799726369.jpg">© AP - Hamideh Shafieeha </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Morocco steps up border security over fears of new mass crossing into Ceuta</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260813-morocco-steps-up-border-security-over-fears-of-new-mass-crossing-into-ceuta</link><description>
Morocco has stepped up security along its borders with the Spanish enclaves of Ceuta and Melilla after fresh calls appeared on social media urging migrants to attempt another mass crossing, weeks after tens of thousands rushed the frontier.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/23e048d2-9012-11f1-878b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-04T060208Z-1711876709-RC27RMAUMI0M-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/23e048d2-9012-11f1-878b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-04T060208Z-1711876709-RC27RMAUMI0M-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3276abb4-96ef-11f1-a5ad-b3954165afe0</guid><pubDate>Thu, 13 Aug 2026 11:59:00 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/23e048d2-9012-11f1-878b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-04T060208Z-1711876709-RC27RMAUMI0M-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg">© Violeta Santos Moura / Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Can UK's hard-right Farage bin financial probe with by-election win?</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260813-can-uk-s-hard-right-farage-bin-financial-probe-with-snap-poll</link><description>
Nigel Farage – leader of the anti-immigration Reform UK party – will be fighting for his parliamentary seat on Thursday, going head to head with parody candidate Count Binface in snap polls. The by-election was called after Farage resigned amid a probe into his finances. But the surprise move threatens to backfire as none of the major political parties has fielded a candidate.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/60be50ba-7c4d-11f1-ba13-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26170105297546.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/60be50ba-7c4d-11f1-ba13-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26170105297546.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f7d7d4b0-9635-11f1-a27e-35fc75775395</guid><pubDate>Thu, 13 Aug 2026 05:38:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/60be50ba-7c4d-11f1-ba13-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26170105297546.jpg">© Jon Super / AP Photo</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Farage wins UK by-election as Count Binface claims 'moral victory'</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260813-farage-wins-uk-by-election-as-count-binface-claims-moral-victory</link><description>
Hard-right British politician Nigel Farage reclaimed his seat in a by-election, according to the final tally Friday, though his main rival and joke candidate Count Binface took an larger than expected share of the ballot.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f50c945a-97ac-11f1-8012-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/78f883b2cf1f30f756558a7c5f4e0c7c88ce82bb.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f50c945a-97ac-11f1-8012-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/78f883b2cf1f30f756558a7c5f4e0c7c88ce82bb.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">592a3810-96be-11f1-9b66-8f0088c55881</guid><pubDate>Thu, 13 Aug 2026 02:26:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f50c945a-97ac-11f1-8012-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/78f883b2cf1f30f756558a7c5f4e0c7c88ce82bb.jpg">© Henry NICHOLLS / AFP/File</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Iran faces growing isolation and uncertain future amid 'dire' economic situation</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260812-iran-faces-growing-isolation-and-uncertain-future-amid-dire-economic-situation</link><description>
As economic pressure mounts in Iran, RFI spoke to economist Djamchid Assadi about how this is leaving the country more isolated and strengthening the role of the Revolutionary Guards.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4809d656-9567-11f1-ae93-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26222573053694.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4809d656-9567-11f1-ae93-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26222573053694.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">94c5695e-9627-11f1-8ead-1f957f32f043</guid><pubDate>Wed, 12 Aug 2026 18:48:01 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4809d656-9567-11f1-ae93-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26222573053694.jpg">AP Photo/Vahid Salemi - Vahid Salemi</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Russia threatens retaliatory seizures of EU ships amid new sanctions push</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260812-russia-threatens-retaliatory-seizures-of-eu-ships-amid-new-sanctions-push</link><description>
Russian President Vladimir Putin on Wednesday threatened to seize ships belonging to European countries in retaliation for plans to sell off cargo seized from Russian "shadow fleet" vessels.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/752422d0-43bf-11f1-af7d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-04-10T150401Z-1458626657-RC2BMKACFUWW-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ESTONIA-SHADOW-FLEET.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/752422d0-43bf-11f1-af7d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-04-10T150401Z-1458626657-RC2BMKACFUWW-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ESTONIA-SHADOW-FLEET.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e58d70ac-964a-11f1-b3ed-8940524ed401</guid><pubDate>Wed, 12 Aug 2026 15:52:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/752422d0-43bf-11f1-af7d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-04-10T150401Z-1458626657-RC2BMKACFUWW-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ESTONIA-SHADOW-FLEET.jpg">© Ints Kalnins / Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Hungary elects Orban critic Andras Baka as first president in new political era</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260812-hungary-elects-orban-critic-andras-baka-as-first-president-of-new-political-era</link><description>
Hungarian lawmakers on Tuesday approved former supreme court chief Andras Baka – a prominent critic of Viktor Orban who was ousted during the ex-premier's time in power – as the country's next head of state.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/44e5b510-9613-11f1-b9fe-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26223528576693.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/44e5b510-9613-11f1-b9fe-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26223528576693.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">762bbf5c-9613-11f1-a50c-03e5429215e8</guid><pubDate>Wed, 12 Aug 2026 09:36:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/44e5b510-9613-11f1-b9fe-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26223528576693.jpg">Szilard Koszticsak/MTI via AP - Szilard Koszticsak</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Total solar eclipse over Spain to draw millions of viewers across Europe</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260812-total-solar-eclipse-over-spain-to-draw-millions-of-viewers-across-europe</link><description>
Large parts of north and central Spain, plus smaller parts of Portugal, Greenland and Iceland, will see a total solar eclipse on Wednesday – with the phenomenon also visible in the south of France. Starting near the North Pole before tracking south, the total eclipse will last up to two minutes and 18 seconds, with the partial eclipse visible across much of Western Europe, including the United Kingdom, Belgium, Switzerland and northern Italy.
